			<h2>Mission</h2>
			<p>My mission is to foster a nurturing and supportive environment for seniors, aiming to enhance their mental wellness and overall quality of life. Older adults, especially those in long-term care or living independently, face mental health challenges that are often overlooked, and this site exists to make clear, accurate information about those challenges easier to find.</p>
			<p>I am committed to:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Educating and empowering:</strong> giving seniors, caregivers, and families the knowledge to understand and address the mental health challenges older adults face.</li>
				<li><strong>Advocacy:</strong> raising awareness about senior mental health, and pushing back on the assumption that mental health decline is just a normal, untreatable part of aging.</li>
				<li><strong>Collaboration:</strong> working alongside mental health professionals, caregivers, and relevant organizations so the information here stays accurate and current.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Personal Story</h2>
			<p>Hello and welcome! I am Aderonke Agboji, a nurse with a background spanning over two decades in long-term care. That work has shaped everything on this site: the questions I write about are the ones families and residents actually ask me.</p>
			<p>Eager to deepen my understanding and impact, I pursued a Master’s in Dementia Studies, gaining insight into dementia and related mental health issues among seniors. I’m currently pursuing a PhD in Health Sciences, specializing in apathy in dementia care, one of the most common and least understood symptoms families deal with.</p>
			<p>Having dedicated 20 years to long-term care, I’ve witnessed firsthand the transformative power of compassionate care intertwined with informed practice. This site is where I share that experience directly, in plain language.</p>

			<h2>Academic Credentials</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Master’s in Dementia Studies:</strong> focused on understanding dementia and related mental health issues among seniors.</li>
				<li><strong>PhD in Health Sciences (ongoing):</strong> specializing in care for people with apathy in community and long-term care settings.</li>
			</ul>
